            <div class="main-content">
                <h2>Expert Care for Hair & Nail Conditions</h2>
                <p>Hair and nail disorders can be distressing and may indicate underlying health issues. At Smart Skin Dermatology, our board-certified dermatologists have extensive experience diagnosing and treating a wide range of hair and nail conditions.</p>
                
                <h3>Hair Conditions We Treat</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Androgenetic Alopecia:</strong> Male and female pattern hair loss, the most common cause of hair thinning</li>
                    <li><strong>Alopecia Areata:</strong> Patchy hair loss caused by autoimmune factors</li>
                    <li><strong>Telogen Effluvium:</strong> Temporary hair shedding due to stress, illness, or hormonal changes</li>
                    <li><strong>Traction Alopecia:</strong> Hair loss from tight hairstyles or hair treatments</li>
                    <li><strong>Scalp Conditions:</strong> Seborrheic dermatitis, scalp psoriasis, and folliculitis</li>
                    <li><strong>Excessive Hair Growth (Hirsutism):</strong> Unwanted facial or body hair</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Hair Loss Treatment Options</h3>
                <p>We offer multiple approaches to address hair loss:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Topical Medications:</strong> Minoxidil and other prescription solutions</li>
                    <li><strong>Oral Medications:</strong> Finasteride, spironolactone, and other systemic treatments</li>
                    <li><strong>Platelet-Rich Plasma (PRP):</strong> Using your body's growth factors to stimulate hair regrowth</li>
                    <li><strong>Corticosteroid Injections:</strong> For alopecia areata and inflammatory conditions</li>
                    <li><strong>Lifestyle & Nutritional Counseling:</strong> Addressing underlying factors</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Nail Conditions We Treat</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Nail Fungus (Onychomycosis):</strong> Fungal infections causing thick, discolored nails</li>
                    <li><strong>Psoriatic Nails:</strong> Pitting, discoloration, and nail bed separation from psoriasis</li>
                    <li><strong>Ingrown Toenails:</strong> Painful nails growing into surrounding skin</li>
                    <li><strong>Nail Trauma:</strong> Injuries affecting nail growth and appearance</li>
                    <li><strong>Nail Dystrophy:</strong> Abnormal nail shape or texture</li>
                    <li><strong>Nail Tumors:</strong> Benign and malignant growths under or around nails</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Nail Treatment Options</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Topical Antifungals:</strong> Prescription-strength nail lacquers and solutions</li>
                    <li><strong>Oral Antifungals:</strong> Systemic medications for stubborn infections</li>
                    <li><strong>Laser Therapy:</strong> Advanced treatment for nail fungus</li>
                    <li><strong>Surgical Procedures:</strong> Nail removal or correction when needed</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>When to See a Dermatologist</h3>
                <p>Schedule an appointment if you notice:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Sudden or patchy hair loss</li>
                    <li>Excessive shedding or thinning</li>
                    <li>Scalp irritation, redness, or scaling</li>
                    <li>Discolored, thick, or crumbling nails</li>
                    <li>Dark streaks or spots under nails</li>
                    <li>Painful or recurrent ingrown nails</li>
                </ul>
