<section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What causes hair loss?</h3>
            <p>Hair loss can result from genetics, hormonal changes, medical conditions, medications, stress, or nutritional deficiencies. A proper diagnosis is essential for effective treatment.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How long does it take to treat nail fungus?</h3>
            <p>Nail fungus treatment typically takes 3-6 months for fingernails and 6-12 months for toenails, as you must wait for the new, healthy nail to grow out completely.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is PRP effective for hair loss?</h3>
            <p>PRP has shown promising results for many patients with androgenetic alopecia, typically requiring 3-4 initial treatments followed by maintenance sessions every 4-6 months.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
